    "result_text": "Full suite green: **292 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation by mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` pattern in this codebase:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean sharesHousehold` field with getter/setter (not persisted; computed at creation, like `namesakeCount`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes it and MapStruct auto-maps it.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, set the flag before saving via a new `sharesHousehold(address, city)` helper that returns `true` when an existing owner already has the same address **and** city (case-insensitive, matching the codebase's comparison conventions). Computed on the raw input before `resolveCity` runs, and creation still proceeds regardless.\n\nThe `Cp17Tests` acceptance test reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` within the same `@Transactional` test \u2014 the spring-data-jpa persistence context returns the same managed instance, so the transient value survives the read (same mechanism `namesakeCount`/`Cp16Tests` relies on). First owner at an address \u2192 `false`; a second at the same address+city \u2192 `true`.",
